    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mrs. Fletcher moved to recommit to the Committee on Energy and Commerce. (text: CR H518)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H34400",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "10:32:11",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House adopted the amendment as agreed to by the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H35000",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "10:31:54",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32600",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "10:30:38",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House rose from the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union to report H.R. 485.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "10:20:08",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H. Res. 996, the Committee of the Whole proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the Molinaro amendment No. 1.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "09:16:25",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - The Committee of the Whole proceeded with one hour of general debate on H.R. 485.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32400",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "09:15:29",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The Speaker designated the Honorable Daniel Meuser to act as Chairman of the Committee.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32020",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "09:15:28",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "House resolved itself into the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union pursuant to H. Res. 996 and Rule XVIII.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "09:15:02",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule provides for consideration of H. Res. 863 and H.R. 485. The resolution provides for consideration of H. Res. 863 under a closed rule and H.R. 485 under a structured rule. The rule provides for two hours of general debate on H. Res. 863 and one hour of general debate on H.R. 485. One motion to recommit allowed on H.R. 485. The resolution further provides that upon adoption H. Res. 863, H. Res. 995 is considered adopted; and further, that no other resolution incidental to impeachment relating to H. Res. 863 shall be privileged during the remainder of the 118th Congress.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-07",
   "actionTime": "09:14:57",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 996. (consideration: CR H515-519; text: CR H515-516)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L220",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-06",
   "actionTime": "14:11:23",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule H. Res. 996 passed House.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "2024-02-05",
   "actionTime": "21:38:03",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 996 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H. Res. 863 and H.R. 485. The resolution provides for consideration of H. Res. 863 under a closed rule and H.R. 485 under a structured rule. The rule provides for two hours of general debate on H. Res. 863 and one hour of general debate on H.R. 485. One motion to recommit allowed on H.R. 485. The resolution further provides that upon adoption H. Res. 863, H. Res. 995 is considered adopted; and further, that no other resolution incidental to impeachment relating to H. Res. 863 shall be privileged during the remainder of the 118th Congress.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
